	(text "Bus pull-ups: 10k to 3.3 V always (the LSFs' B side), 2.2k switched by the co-processor (GPIO10–13, 16–19); the ±5 V rails into the ADC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 316.23 261.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "31791d01-bd4d-5cdb-9769-3a604146d55f")
	)
	(text_box "GPIO2–9 = buses A–H (gusmanb CH1–8, 8-bit mode); GPIO0 → GPIO1 bridged (its trigger path).\nGPIO14 = the node's mark (TCA9535 U6 P14); GPIO25 = LED; GPIO19…16, 13…10 = pull-up enables A…H (2.2k);\nGPIO40–45 = VREF 1–6 / 2 (through 100k); GPIO46 = +5V_MX × 47/147;\n  GPIO47 = 3.3 V − (3.3 + 5) × 10/110 from −5 V (2.55 V nominal).  The ADC's eight inputs all used.\nRUN pulled up, BOOTSEL (QSPI_SS) through 1k: both held by the node (TCA9534A), open drain.\nUSB on the hub's port 7 (Full Speed, 22 Ω).\nCore regulator: Raspberry Pi's Minimal R4 block turned 180°; L1's dot (pad 1) on +1V1, not VREG_LX.\nC47 (DVDD pin 32, furthest from the regulator) 4.7 µF; no copper under LX / L1 (In1, In2, B.Cu)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 309.88 0)
		(size 284.48 22.86)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
